{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01En6VbUnUnsMFaUsJhwgXq5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd052-tty\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/tty: Print Terminal File Name\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Scripts use tty to determine whether stdin is connected to a terminal and to obtain the\n6\t  terminal device name. The -s (silent) flag suppresses output and reports only via exit\n7\t  code, which is useful in conditional expressions. The Go implementation must match the\n8\t  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtty, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout\n9\t  and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print the file name of the terminal connected to stdin.\n13\t  - G2: Support the -s (silent) flag for exit-code-only operation.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default behavior and silent mode\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments and stdin is a terminal, must print the terminal device name (e.g., /dev/ttys000) followed by a newline and exit 0.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: When invoked with no arguments and stdin is not a terminal, must print \"not a tty\" followed by a newline and exit 1.\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"-s (--silent, --quiet) must suppress all output. The exit code is 0 if stdin is a terminal, 1 otherwise.\"\n25\t\n26\t  R2:\n27\t    title: Error handling\n28\t    items:\n29\t      - R2.1:\n30\t          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 2.\n31\t      - R2.2:\n32\t          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 2.\n33\t\n34\t  R3:\n35\t    title: Differential testing\n36\t    items:\n37\t      - R3.1:\n38\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gtty) via pkg/testutils.\n39\t      - R3.2:\n40\t          text: \"Tests must cover: stdin connected to a terminal (if available), stdin redirected from a file or pipe (not a tty), -s flag, and error cases.\"\n41\t      - R3.3:\n42\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n43\t\n44\tnon_goals:\n45\t  - cmd/tty does not configure terminal settings; use stty for that.\n46\t  - cmd/tty does not check terminals connected to stdout or stderr; it checks stdin only.\n47\t\n48\tacceptance_criteria:\n49\t  - id: AC1\n50\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/tty with stdin from a pipe prints \\\"not a tty\\\" and exits 1, matching gtty.\"\n51\t    traces:\n52\t      - R1.1\n53\t      - R1.2\n54\t      - R1.3\n55\t      - R2.1\n56\t      - R2.2\n57\t      - R3.1\n58\t      - R3.2\n59\t  - id: AC2\n60\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/tty -s with stdin from a pipe produces no output and exits 1, matching gtty.\"\n61\t    traces:\n62\t      - R1.1\n63\t      - R1.2\n64\t      - R1.3\n65\t      - R2.1\n66\t      - R2.2\n67\t      - R3.1\n68\t      - R3.2\n69\t  - id: AC3\n70\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gtty passes for piped and terminal stdin cases.\"\n71\t    traces:\n72\t      - R1.1\n73\t      - R1.2\n74\t      - R1.3\n75\t      - R3.1\n76\t      - R3.2\n77\t      - R3.3\n78\t  - id: AC4\n79\t    criterion: \"cmd/tty compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n80\t    traces:\n81\t      - R1.1\n82\t      - R1.2\n83\t      - R1.3\n84\t      - R2.1\n85\t      - R2.2\n86\t      - R3.1\n87\t      - R3.2\n88\t      - R3.3\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23675902-9945-4efc-adaf-76a5c2d16eb3","uuid":"14f4cf59-e517-41b3-a946-93cbc8648b51","timestamp":"2026-05-15T00:35:39.529Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5233/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd052-tty.yaml","content":"id: srd052-tty\ntitle: \"cmd/tty: Print Terminal File Name\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Scripts use tty to determine whether stdin is connected to a terminal and to obtain the\n  terminal device name. The -s (silent) flag suppresses output and reports only via exit\n  code, which is useful in conditional expressions. The Go implementation must match the\n  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtty, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout\n  and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the file name of the terminal connected to stdin.\n  - G2: Support the -s (silent) flag for exit-code-only operation.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior and silent mode\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments and stdin is a terminal, must print the terminal device name (e.g., /dev/ttys000) followed by a newline and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments and stdin is not a terminal, must print \"not a tty\" followed by a newline and exit 1.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-s (--silent, --quiet) must suppress all output. The exit code is 0 if stdin is a terminal, 1 otherwise.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 2.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 2.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gtty) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: stdin connected to a terminal (if available), stdin redirected from a file or pipe (not a tty), -s flag, and error cases.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/tty does not configure terminal settings; use stty for that.\n  - cmd/tty does not check terminals connected to stdout or stderr; it checks stdin only.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/tty with stdin from a pipe prints \\\"not a tty\\\" and exits 1, matching gtty.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/tty -s with stdin from a pipe produces no output and exits 1, matching gtty.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gtty passes for piped and terminal stdin cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/tty compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
