{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing stitch task #5233: implementing cmd/tty features for srd052-tty requirements R2.2 and R3.1-R3.3. Specifically:\n   - **R2.2**: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 2 (may already be implemented in existing code)\n   - **R3.1**: Create differential tests comparing Go tty binary against GNU gtty reference binary via pkg/testutils\n   - **R3.2**: Tests must cover: stdin from pipe (not a tty), -s flag, and error cases (unknown flags, extra operands)\n   - **R3.3**: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/tty/main.go` (complete implementation) and `cmd/tty/tty_test.go` (create new differential test file).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `testutils.BuildBinary`, `exec.LookPath(\"gtty\")`, `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - DiffTest struct: `{ Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n   - Graceful skip when reference binary (gtty) is not installed\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for locale-independent comparison\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - CGo usage for `ttyname()` syscall\n   - GNU coreutils error message format for unknown flags\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd052-tty.yaml**\n     - Full SRD with requirements R1 (default behavior/silent mode), R2 (error handling), R3 (differential testing)\n     - R2.2: \"Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 2.\"\n     - R3.1-R3.3: Differential testing requirements with gtty, covering pipe stdin, -s flag, errors, LC_ALL=C\n   \n   - **cmd/tty/main.go** (existing, 103 lines)\n     - Already implements R1.1-R2.1 per package comment\n     - Uses cgo: `#include <unistd.h>` for `C.ttyname()`\n     - R2.2 appears already implemented:\n       - Unknown long flags (lines 76-79): `tty: unrecognized option '%s'` → exit 2\n       - Invalid short flags (lines 96-99): `tty: invalid option -- '%c'` → exit 2\n       - Extra operands (lines 61-64, 83-85): `tty: extra operand '%s'` → exit 2\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd052-tty R1.1-R2.1.\n     package main\n     \n     /*\n     #include <unistd.h>\n     */\n     import \"C\"\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: tty [OPTION]...\n     Print the file name of the terminal connected to standard input.\n     \n       -s, --silent, --quiet   print nothing, only return an exit status\n           --help     display this help and exit\n           --version  output version information and exit\n     `\n     \n     const versionText = `tty (go-unix-utils) dev\n     `\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         silent := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         isTTY := sys.IsTerminal(os.Stdin.Fd())\n         if !silent {\n             if isTTY {\n                 name := C.ttyname(C.int(os.Stdin.Fd()))\n                 if name == nil {\n                     fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, \"not a tty\")\n                 } else if _, err := fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, C.GoString(name)); err != nil {\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n             } else {\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, \"not a tty\")\n             }\n         }\n         if !isTTY {\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func parseArgs(args []string) bool {\n         silent := false\n         endOfFlags := false\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             if endOfFlags {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tty: extra operand '%s'\\n\", arg)\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'tty --help' for more information.\")\n                 os.Exit(2)\n             }\n             switch {\n             case arg == \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case arg == \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case arg == \"--silent\", arg == \"--quiet\":\n                 silent = true\n             case arg == \"--\":\n                 endOfFlags = true\n             case strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\"):\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tty: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", arg)\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'tty --help' for more information.\")\n                 os.Exit(2)\n             case strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") && len(arg) > 1:\n                 silent = parseShortFlags(arg[1:], silent)\n             default:\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tty: extra operand '%s'\\n\", arg)\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'tty --help' for more information.\")\n                 os.Exit(2)\n             }\n         }\n         return silent\n     }\n     \n     func parseShortFlags(flags string, silent bool) bool {\n         for _, ch := range flags {\n             switch ch {\n             case 's':\n                 silent = true\n             default:\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tty: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", ch)\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'tty --help' for more information.\")\n                 os.Exit(2)\n             }\n         }\n         return silent\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Determined that R2.2 (unknown flags error handling) appears already implemented in the existing main.go code. The parseArgs function handles unknown long flags (lines 76-79) and parseShortFlags handles unknown short flags (lines 96-99), both printing to stderr and exiting 2.\n   - The main remaining work is creating the test file (R3.1-R3.3) and updating the package comment to reflect R2.2 coverage.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial massive stitch task prompt with full project context, task description, constraints, SRDs, architecture, constitutions, and requirements for task #5233: `[stitch] cmd/tty: features implementation (srd052-tty R2.2-R3.3)`\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Update `cmd/tty/main.go` package comment from \"R1.1-R2.1\" to \"R1.1-R2.2\" (since R2.2 is already implemented)\n   - Create `cmd/tty/tty_test.go` with differential tests (R3.1-R3.3) covering:\n     - No args with piped stdin → \"not a tty\\n\", exit 1\n     - `-s` flag with piped stdin → no output, exit 1\n     - Unknown long flag `--invalid` → error to stderr, exit 2\n     - Unknown short flag `-x` → error to stderr, exit 2\n     - Extra operand → error to stderr, exit 2\n     - All with LC_ALL=C environment\n   - Run `go build -o bin/tty ./cmd/tty/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/tty/...` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/tty/... -count=1` to verify tests pass/skip\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two required files (srd052-tty.yaml and cmd/tty/main.go) and was about to begin implementation. I had completed step 1 (review context) and was partway through step 2 (plan approach) when the summary was requested. No code has been written or modified yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/tty/tty_test.go` with the differential test file and update the package comment in `cmd/tty/main.go` to reflect R2.2 coverage, then compile and test. The test file should use:\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to build the Go binary\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gtty\")` with `t.Skip` if not foun