{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HKZtrM7UCDVzmiKm4VTE4L","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Here's what I found:\n\n## DiffTest Struct Definition\n\nThe `DiffTest` struct is defined in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5233/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` with these fields:\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string\n\tArgs          []string\n\tStdin         []byte\n\tEnv           []string\n\tWorkDir       string\n\tExitCode      int\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n```\n\n**Field explanations:**\n- **Name**: Identifies the subtest (used with t.Run)\n- **Args**: Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n- **Stdin**: Input stream (nil means EOF, empty non-nil slice represents open stdin immediately closed)\n- **Env**: Environment variables (nil means inherit test process environment with LC_ALL=C applied)\n- **WorkDir**: Working directory for execution (defaults to t.TempDir() if empty)\n- **ExitCode**: Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n- **Normalize**: Slice of NormalizeFunc applied in order to stdout/stderr before comparison\n- **ExpectedFiles**: Map of relative file paths to expected byte content\n\n## Example Test File\n\nHere's the full test file for the `true` command at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5233/cmd/true/true_test.go`:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gtrue\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n\t}\n\tdiscardStdout := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:     \"no-args\",\n\t\t\tExitCode: 0,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:     \"arbitrary-args\",\n\t\t\tArgs:     []string{\"foo\", \"bar\", \"--baz\"},\n\t\t\tExitCode: 0,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:     \"help\",\n\t\t\tArgs:     []string{\"--help\"},\n\t\t\tExitCode: 0,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:     \"version\",\n\t\t\tArgs:     []string{\"--version\"},\n\t\t\tExitCode: 0,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\nThe pattern is straightforward: build the Go binary, find the GNU reference binary (gtrue in this case), define test cases using the `DiffTest` struct, and call `RunDiffTests` with the binaries and test cases. The framework compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the two implementations."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23675902-9945-4efc-adaf-76a5c2d16eb3","uuid":"ec6b4a09-9be2-425d-9d52-f4fc8c5bfebb","timestamp":"2026-05-15T00:37:05.266Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5233, find the DiffTest struct definition in pkg/testutils/ and show me the full struct fields. Also find one example test file in cmd/ that uses RunDiffTests so I can see the pattern. Show the full test file content for a simple utility (like cmd/true or cmd/false or cmd/yes — something small).","agentId":"aec569fec28844774","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Here's what I found:\n\n## DiffTest Struct Definition\n\nThe `DiffTest` struct is defined in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5233/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` with these fields:\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string\n\tArgs          []string\n\tStdin         []byte\n\tEnv           []string\n\tWorkDir       string\n\tExitCode      i